<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n41414" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">restĭo</span></b> , ōnis,
			m.
		restis. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A ropemaker</i>, <i>rope-seller</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Suet. Aug. 2 <i>fin.</i></span></i>;
			cf. <i><span class="en">Fronto, p. 2201</span></i>
			P.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, in a comic lusus verbb., with
			bucaeda, for <i>one who is scourged with ropes</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Plaut.
				Most. 4, 2, 2</span></i>. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>The title of a poem by Laberius</i>, <i><span class="en">Gell. 10,
				17, 2</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
